<p>Reports <code>@EventListener</code> methods that handle Spring Boot application events which are published
  <b>before the <code>ApplicationContext</code> is created</b>. Such events can never be delivered to a bean-registered
  listener, so the annotated method silently never runs.</p>

<p>The affected events are:</p>
<ul>
  <li><code>ApplicationStartingEvent</code></li>
  <li><code>ApplicationEnvironmentPreparedEvent</code></li>
  <li><code>ApplicationContextInitializedEvent</code></li>
  <li><code>ApplicationPreparedEvent</code></li>
</ul>

<p><b>Example:</b></p>
<pre><code lang="java">
  @Component
  class MyListener {
    @EventListener // reports: this event is published before the context exists
    void on(ApplicationStartingEvent event) { ... }
  }
</code></pre>

<p>To listen for these early events, register the listener via <code>META-INF/spring.factories</code>
  (<code>org.springframework.context.ApplicationListener</code>) or
  <code>SpringApplication.addListeners(...)</code> instead of relying on a bean.</p>
